  "description": "Seattle GiveCamp is a free, in-person weekend hackathon where developers, designers, and project managers build real software for Seattle-area nonprofits — completely pro bono. Since 2011, we have served 150+ nonprofits with free tech work worth hundreds of thousands of dollars a year. No entry fee and no sponsor pitches — you show up, join a team, and ship something useful for your community. When: October 16–18, 2026 (Friday evening – Sunday) Where: Microsoft Building 122, 15120 NE 40th St, Redmond, WA 98052 (in person) Who: All skill levels welcome — developers, designers, project managers, DBAs, DevOps engineers, and technical writers.",
